  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Saat-Aath (7-8). Sequence: deal 5 each -> non-dealer calls trump -> deal 5 down + 5 up tableau each -> play 15 follow-suit tricks with special trumps 7H/7S -> score by quotas (dealer >7, non-dealer >8, exact 7-8 tie).',
    Player: 'Saat-Aath is a two-player race across 15 tricks. The non-dealer calls trump, special sevens become top trumps, and you manage both hand cards and exposed table cards. Hit your quota while denying your opponent theirs.',
    objective: 'Win enough tricks relative to your role quota: dealer targets more than 7, non-dealer targets more than 8, and 7-8 exact is a tie.',
    gameplay: '1. **Lead**: Non-dealer leads first trick. 2. **Follow suit**: Second player must follow suit if possible from hand or currently face-up table cards. 3. **If void**: Any available card may be played; trumps can cut. 4. **Trick winner**: Higher card of same suit wins, otherwise trump wins, otherwise first played card wins when neither card is trump. 5. **Card availability**: You may play from hand or any face-up table card; when a face-up table card is played, its face-down undercard is revealed for future tricks. 6. **Continuation**: Winner of each trick leads next. 7. **End**: After 15 tricks, compare trick totals against quota thresholds.',
    keyRules: [
      '7 of hearts and 7 of spades are always top trumps when special-sevens rule is used.',
      'Those two sevens count as trumps, not as hearts/spades for follow-suit in non-trump suits.',
      'Second hand must follow suit if able; otherwise may discard or trump.',
      'Exact 7 tricks for dealer and 8 for non-dealer is a draw.',
      'Non-dealer always chooses trump after the initial 5-card deal.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Exactly 2 players; dealer alternates by deal.',
      deck: 'Start from 52 cards and remove all 2-6 plus 7 of clubs and 7 of diamonds. Trumps rank: 7 of hearts (highest), 7 of spades, then A K Q J 10 9 8 of trump suit. Non-trump suits rank A K Q J 10 9 8.',
      equipment: '30-card pack and optional score sheet for match play.',
      dealing: 'Dealer gives 5 hand cards to each player. Non-dealer calls trump. Dealer then deals 5 face-down table cards in a row to each player and places 1 face-up card on each stack, giving each player 15 playable cards over time.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Lead**: Non-dealer leads first trick. 2. **Follow suit**: Second player must follow suit if possible from hand or currently face-up table cards. 3. **If void**: Any available card may be played; trumps can cut. 4. **Trick winner**: Higher card of same suit wins, otherwise trump wins, otherwise first played card wins when neither card is trump. 5. **Card availability**: You may play from hand or any face-up table card; when a face-up table card is played, its face-down undercard is revealed for future tricks. 6. **Continuation**: Winner of each trick leads next. 7. **End**: After 15 tricks, compare trick totals against quota thresholds.',
